<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Timoleon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 411–<a href="/years/334-bce">334 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Timoleon was a Corinthian statesman and general sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in 344 BCE to help Syracuse. He drove out the tyrant Dionysius II, defeated a large Carthaginian army at the Crimissus river around 339 BCE and overthrew tyrants in other Greek cities. He resettled ruined cities such as Gela and Acragas with new colonists, then retired and died in Syracuse around 334 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/timoleon.jpg" alt="Timoleon" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown / Photography: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silver_stater,_Syracuse,_Timoleon,_344-337_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
